---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro'
---

<Layout 
  title="Git Cheat Sheet | Free Branching, Rebasing & Workflow Reference"
  description="Complete Git cheat sheet with branching, rebasing, stashing, undoing changes, and common workflows. Free reference for developers."
>
  <section class="hero">
    <h1>Git<br><span>Cheat Sheet</span></h1>
    <p>Branching, rebasing, stashing, undoing changes, and common workflows. From basics to advanced Git.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Setup &amp; Basics</h2>
    <div class="formula-grid">
      <div class="formula-card">
        <h3>Configuration</h3>
        <pre><code>git config --global user.name "Your Name"
git config --global user.email "you@email.com"
git config --global init.defaultBranch main
git config --list</code></pre>
      </div>
      <div class="formula-card">
        <h3>Creating Repos</h3>
        <pre><code>git init                 # new repo
git clone url            # clone remote
git clone --depth 1 url  # shallow clone

# .gitignore essentials
node_modules/
.env
*.log
dist/</code></pre>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Staging &amp; Commits</h3>
    <div class="formula-grid">
      <div class="formula-card">
        <h3>Staging Changes</h3>
        <pre><code>git status
git add file.txt        # stage one file
git add -p              # stage interactively
git add .               # stage all changes
git reset HEAD file.txt # unstage</code></pre>
      </div>
      <div class="formula-card">
        <h3>Commit Messages</h3>
        <pre><code>git commit -m "feat: add user auth"
git commit --amend -m "better message"
git commit --amend --no-edit  # keep message

# Conventional commits:
# feat:  new feature
# fix:   bug fix
# docs:  documentation
# refactor: code restructuring</code></pre>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Branching</h2>
    <div class="formula-grid">
      <div class="formula-card">
        <h3>Create &amp; Switch</h3>
        <pre><code>git branch feature/login
git switch feature/login
git switch -c new-branch   # create + switch
git branch -d old-branch   # delete merged
git branch -D old-branch   # force delete
git branch -a              # list all</code></pre>
      </div>
      <div class="formula-card">
        <h3>Merging</h3>
        <pre><code>git switch main
git merge feature/login
git merge --squash feature/login
git merge --no-ff feature/login

# Abort a merge
git merge --abort</code></pre>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Rebasing &amp; History</h2>
    <div class="formula-grid">
      <div class="formula-card">
        <h3>Interactive Rebase</h3>
        <pre><code># Rebase last 3 commits
git rebase -i HEAD~3

# Commands:
# pick   = keep commit
# squash = merge into prev
# drop   = remove commit
# edit   = modify commit</code></pre>
      </div>
      <div class="formula-card">
        <h3>Stashing</h3>
        <pre><code>git stash                    # stash changes
git stash push -m "WIP"     # named stash
git stash list               # view stash
git stash pop                # apply + remove
git stash apply stash@{2}   # apply specific</code></pre>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Undoing Changes</h2>
    <div class="formula-grid">
      <div class="formula-card">
        <h3>Discard &amp; Restore</h3>
        <pre><code>git restore file.txt           # discard
git restore --staged file.txt  # unstage
git restore --source=HEAD~3 file.txt

# Undo last commit (keep changes)
git reset HEAD~1

# Undo last commit (discard changes)
git reset --hard HEAD~1</code></pre>
      </div>
      <div class="formula-card">
        <h3>Reverting</h3>
        <pre><code>git revert HEAD          # undo last commit
git revert abc1234       # undo specific

# Safely undo pushed commits
# Creates a new commit that reverses
git revert HEAD~3..HEAD</code></pre>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Download</h2>
    <p>Print this page or save as PDF for quick reference.</p>
    <p><strong>Tip:</strong> Use Ctrl+P (Cmd+P on Mac) to print or save as PDF.</p>
  </section>
</Layout>
